n the way you were covered or  johnny rackler was covered as opposed to  the way chairman adam schiff was covered  look we we talk a lot about  democracy and and how democracy is  undercut  through different actions which i think  is really healthy but  there's no other uh thing that you can  say  undercuts democracy than a press that is  not  unbiased and an entire press corps in  washington dc that cheerleads  and is partisan that's a really recipe  for disaster when you think about  how to hold government to account  how to challenge power  we call this out when we see it in other  countries when you don't have a press  corps  that plays fair that that immediately  goes  for uh one side and protects that one  side at all costs  i also think we have to get to the point  those of us on the outside of washington  dc  we have to be smarter about what we're  asking washington dc to do because in  many ways i think we're asking them to  reform themselves  including the washington d.c press court  they all live there they work there they  go to school there they go to church  there they know each other  their social circle is dependent upon  each other and so  those of us on the outside we continue  to say oh these reporters need to be  unbiased and and they need to uh push  and hold the government accountable i  actually think we're at the point where  they're never going to do that and so  why do we keep pushing them to do it i  think we've got to start doing  it on our own which is where social  media becomes such an important tool  is to be able to check government and  push  out uh the facts as we see it let's not  rely on the media anymore because the  media  failed us and we got to stop asking them  to do something that i just  fundamentally don't think they'll ever  do  sir we have about 30 seconds what what  what should a careful  observer be looking for in in the early  days of joe biden's administration to  see whether or not the media  is going to do its job